WEBVTT

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:17.950
<i>I need a license! Give me a formal license!</i>

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:21.600
<i>Dammit, give it to me!</i>

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.600
<i>Tange Danpei, you are under arrest for assault.</i>

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.730
<i>Joe!</i>

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.240
What's the matter, Joe?

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.250
What good will seeing the old man do?

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:49.820
O-Of course it'll do some good!

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.640
We've already come all this way, Joe.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.260
The old man must be hungry and waiting for us.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.820
This is for Tange Danpei?

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:19.350
Y-Yes, we were hoping you could take it to him.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.320
And may we request a meeting?

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.160
That won't be necessary.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.530
Tange Danpei has just been released.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.120
Released?

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.290
S-So who bailed him out?

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.800
It's been a while, everyone.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.010
M-Miss!

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:45.020
You guys had better be grateful.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:50.160
The young lady came here to bail Tange Danpei out after reading about him in the paper.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.270
R-Really?

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:53.760
Th-Thank you so...

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.320
Well, well, well...

00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:58.930
Not like it makes a difference now,

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.320
but this is what we call "meddling."

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.830
Joe! Joe!

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:07.630
Now that he's banned from the boxing association, the old man is nothing more than a walking corpse.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:08.730
Joe!

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:09.540
Am I not right?

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:14.750
So what do you think you're doing, bringing that corpse out in public?

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:15.740
Huh?

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:18.120
A corpse? I'm not so sure.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.590
But Danpei-san looked very pleased with himself.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:22.290
Pleased?

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.100
Really?

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.020
O-Old man!

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.060
Oh! You guys!

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.160
Th-Thank goodness, old man!

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.140
It's good to see you again, Danpei-san.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:44.580
Well, Miss... It seems that against my will, I'm in your debt again.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.860
How can I ever repay you?

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:51.230
You really didn't have to...

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.160
He's happy.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.080
What does he have to be happy about?

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.090
Now let's go, Yabuki-kun.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:06.090
Joe, Shiraki Mikinosuke-san wants to talk to us.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:08.100
Talk to us?

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:09.550
Yes.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.650
We're here. Go right ahead.

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:29.580
What have we got here?

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.680
This is your first time here, isn't it?

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.840
This is the Shiraki Gym.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.760
I've heard about it before...

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.420
but I never imagined it would be this grand!

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:47.550
This isn't so much a gym as it is a five-star apartment block!

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.560
Well isn't that something...?

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:57.070
"The most blessed, modern gym in all of the Orient." That's our catchphrase.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:00.140
Now that's impressive.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:03.890
This is like night and day compared to the Tange Boxing Club at the Namida Bridge!

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:05.710
I-I have a request, Miss.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.490
May we have a tour of the place later?

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:09.980
Yes. Once my grandfather's business with you is settled,

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:11.890
I will show you around the practice grounds.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.940
Rikiishi-kun may even be there.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.220
Oh, Rikiishi-kun?

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:19.860
He's going through a lot right now.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.090
He's the first person from Shiraki Gym to make it to the rookie tournament finals,

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.870
which are only a week away.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:29.920
The media is making a huge fuss, and he's hustling like never before.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.800
Well, from what I can see, he's sure to be the champ.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:40.390
Enter.

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:43.460
Sorry for the wait.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:44.570
I've brought them all here.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.150
Oh, so they've come?

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.530
Now, invite them inside.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.060
This way.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:53.080
It's a pleasure!

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:55.640
Now, take a seat.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:56.820
Oh?

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.080
Where's Yabuki-kun?

00:05:59.160 --> 00:05:59.540
Huh?

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:02.640
Oh, that's strange.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:05.090
He was with us just a second ago...

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:07.630
You don't think he ran away?

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:23.560
Well, time to see how Rikiishi practices.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.980
So as you can see, he throws a right!

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:45.340
And as he does that, he moves his hips back!

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.800
Understand?

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:54.770
This... This really is the greatest gym in the Orient.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.530
Hey, you dirty kid!

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.580
If you're here on a field trip, you better stand in the sidelines!

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:11.080
You're getting in the way of our practice!

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:16.140
I see. Then I'll do that.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.450
I don't want to get in the way of you playing jump rope.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.860
Come on, keep practicing!

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.810
One, two! One, two!

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.310
Y-You dare talk like that to me, bastard!?

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:30.340
What was that?

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.340
What's going on?

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.390
What happened?

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:38.060
Wanna fight? I'll have you know...

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.840
I'm a Four-Rounder! Don't go crying to mommy if you get hurt!

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.150
Sure!

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:47.650
Stop it, you two.

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:53.990
You goddamn idiot!

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.470
Why do you have to raise hell everywhere you go?

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.500
And of all places, in Shiraki-san's...

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.780
Shut up!

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:04.340
I'm not the one who got arrested last night!

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:10.320
We're so sorry for the trouble we've caused, Shiraki-san...

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.020
Don't mention it. Now let's have a chat over tea.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:15.630
Yes... Gladly...

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:19.170
Come on, Joe! Sit down!

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:23.940
You'll have to excuse him. He's never learned his manners.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.660
Now, now, you don't have to make excuses.

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:31.900
I'm sure I would've caused a fuss too, if I were in your shoes.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:34.990
Thank you...

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:39.420
I feel that the boxing association treated you a little too coldly.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:41.840
I've called you here out of kindness.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:45.500
So, are you gonna make the association bastards reconsider?

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.920
Joe... Joe!

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:49.330
That would be nice.

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:52.930
With the chairman of the Shiraki Corporation behind us, the association is sure to listen.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.680
No, I can't do that.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.140
That would be impossible.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:06.740
Tange-kun was denied a license by a majority vote.

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:08.390
There's nothing I can do about that.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:09.900
But...

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:25.420
How would you boys like to train at my Shiraki Gym?

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:32.630
B-But...

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:38.520
A professional trainer needs a license from the commissioner to train publicly.

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:43.470
But, if you were to coach Yabuki-kun from behind the scenes,

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:46.970
no one would object to you building your dreams for tomorrow.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.150
How about it, Tange-kun?

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.380
What the hell?

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.230
Don't I have a say in this?

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.370
You've got to be kidding me!

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.040
I'm not just gonna let you decide for me!

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:02.380
Yabuki-kun!

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:05.540
I saw talent in you while you were in the juvenile prison.

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:12.050
I don't just want that talent for the Shiraki Gym.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:15.740
I want you for the future of Japanese professional boxing!

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:16.550
Please understand.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:45.910
How about it?

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:50.800
If Tange-kun and your friend Nishi-kun would come as well,

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:52.170
it would be a great honor.

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:57.320
Well, myself aside, Joe and Nishi

00:10:57.320 --> 00:11:01.950
will never have their skills blossom at this rate...

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:03.180
So I would be delighted...

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:05.640
Oh! So...

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:18.650
What's the matter, Joe?

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:26.300
The tomorrow... The tomorrow that you thought you'd lost...

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:28.160
is about to come back to you!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:34.050
It seems Yabuki-kun is hung up on something silly.

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:40.800
The thought of being indebted to the Shiraki family irritates him.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.680
He's worried about his honor... or something like that.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:46.140
Shut up! If you know that already, then don't bother talking!

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:47.950
No!

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:49.810
Let me just say one thing!

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.230
My grandfather and I have gone this far

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.650
because we want to make the Shiraki Gym a first-rate gym.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:55.430
So, Yabuki-kun...

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:58.400
Shut up! I'm thinking about it!

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:02.450
Just shut your trap for a second.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:19.090
On one hand, I don't want to be indebted to Yohko.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:25.390
And... the run-down gym under the Namida Bridge suits me far better.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.170
On the other hand...

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:42.480
If...

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:44.860
If I let this chance go...

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:14.560
I've made up my mind.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:16.870
Oh, you've decided?

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:18.560
Joe! Really?

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.570
Yeah.

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:25.570
Excuse me.

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:35.040
Joe!

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:38.540
Well this is a surprise. Everyone's here.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:44.930
I've finished all the paperwork for the rookie tournament finals.

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:47.380
Just thought I'd let you know.

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:50.300
I see. Perfect timing.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:52.390
Rikiishi-kun...

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:54.020
Yes?

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:59.520
I was just asking Yabuki-kun and his friends to join the Shiraki Gym.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:03.230
Oh?

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.780
And?

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:15.960
Be glad, Rikiishi-kun!

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:19.000
Yabuki-kun's just answered our request!

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:20.920
From now on, you two...

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.580
No, that would be three including Nishi-kun...

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:24.520
You will all be partners!

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:26.470
I hope you get along.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:31.330
Is that so?

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:33.020
Thank goodness for that.

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:35.970
Well, I'm quite busy, so excuse me.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:43.980
Doesn't it seem like he's gotten a little bigger?

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:53.820
<i>Be glad, Rikiishi-kun!</i>

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:56.410
<i>You two will be partners!</i>

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:06.440
So, Tange-kun...

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:10.560
How would you two like to start practice tomorrow?

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.840
No use in waiting!

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:14.800
That would be great!

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:16.330
Actually...

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:17.280
I refuse.

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.000
Refuse?

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.440
Y-You don't mean...

00:15:23.350 --> 00:15:26.440
I'd love to join the Shiraki Gym, but I must decline.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.010
Y-Yabuki-kun...

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:30.950
Wh-What's gotten into you, Joe?

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.830
Tell me why, Yabuki-kun!

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:35.720
If you have a condition, I'll hear it!

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.310
I'll do whatever I can!

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:39.710
He's the reason.

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:46.150
When I saw the bastard's face, I remembered something important.

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:49.610
There's a rule that two fighters from the same gym can't compete.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:56.220
You mean that because you want to fight Rikiishi-kun...

00:15:56.820 --> 00:16:01.060
You could say that's my only purpose in life.

00:16:04.370 --> 00:16:06.040
That's easy to say, Joe...

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:11.160
But if you don't join here, you won't be able to do boxing at all, let alone fight Rikiishi-kun!

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:16.600
Rikiishi, we'll settle our score from the juvie in the professional ring!

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:20.370
I swear, that day will come soon!

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:24.960
You'd better look forward to it, and brush up your skills in the meantime!

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.680
Those are big words, coming from an amateur.

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:51.090
Are you calling me an amateur?

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:00.050
Let me go!

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:02.060
Joe, what do you think you're doing?

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:02.730
Come with me!

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:04.430
Let me go, dammit!

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:04.430
<i>Stop it!</i>

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:05.590
Hey, Nishi!

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:07.920
Help me take Joe outside!

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:09.870
Stop this, Joe!

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:10.380
Let me go!

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.880
Stop it! Stop it right now!

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:14.070
Let me go!

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:17.380
We're sorry for causing you trouble.

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:20.890
It was a very kind offer you made us...

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:23.840
but Joe's not going to hear the end of it.

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:28.360
Please forget about what happened today.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:30.400
Let me go, you son of a bitch!

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.920
That's enough out of you, you mongrel!

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:44.790
That's enough out of you, you mongrel!

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:51.220
What do you have to gain from starting trouble here!?

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:54.880
I've had enough of your immature vanity!

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.850
Immature... vanity?

00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:58.560
That's what I said.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:00.270
Crush Rikiishi?

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:01.850
You've got to be kidding!

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:03.770
Let me tell you something...

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:06.550
The guy that Rikiishi was sparring with...

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:10.380
was Kamada, the Japanese Lightweight Champion!

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:11.360
Lightweight?

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.340
That's right!

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:14.010
Rikiishi himself is a featherweight...

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:17.630
but he was sparring with a veteran lightweight, one weight class above him...

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:19.870
and he had the upper hand!

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:23.170
He's nothing like the old Rikiishi!

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:25.140
He's entirely different!

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:28.710
Just let me say one more thing.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:33.340
A foolhardy stray dog like you who flares up when called an amateur...

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:37.140
will only get torn to shreds by a pedigree dog...

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:40.390
and end up a shameful loser.

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.860
Stop, old man!

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:46.890
There are just some things that you shouldn't say!

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:49.100
I-I'm... a loser?

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:50.290
I-I'm... a loser?

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:51.480
I-I'm... a loser?

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:01.990
Wait! Where are you going?

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:06.990
Old man...

00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:10.500
Why don't you just see whether or not that pedigree dog will really tear this stray dog to shreds?

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:15.380
You son of a bitch! Are you blind?

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:22.030
Stop acting like you're my boss!

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:26.270
You're just a worthless bum who can't even get one or two guys into pro boxing!

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:27.890
Joe! No!

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:54.590
You idiot!

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:55.760
Oh God!

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:57.630
This is really, really bad!

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:26.160
Old man, hang in there! Old man!

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:30.370
I take back everything I said.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:31.480
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:32.950
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:34.770
I'm so sorry, old man.

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:46.510
Nishi, help me carry the old man.

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.640
Nishi, help me carry the old man.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.260
Hey. You forgot these.

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:24.990
Mongrel!

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:44.320
Joe...

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:49.600
You finally had found a rainbow leading to tomorrow...

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:51.330
but you rejected it...

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:56.790
It's no use complaining about it now.

00:21:58.650 --> 00:22:00.190
Have you forgotten, old man?

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:02.280
The night I got back,

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:06.750
who was it that said we'd cross the Bridge of Tears in the opposite direction,

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:08.470
not with tears of a loser, but of a winner?

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:11.160
Yes, I said it.

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:12.980
I did say it.

00:22:13.690 --> 00:22:15.760
But now, that bridge...

00:22:15.760 --> 00:22:20.700
that bridge to the boxing association is impassable!

00:22:21.450 --> 00:22:23.870
If there's no bridge, we'll just have to build one...

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:25.240
With our own hands!

00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:30.920
You called me a stray dog, didn't you?

00:22:31.810 --> 00:22:32.790
But...

00:22:32.790 --> 00:22:35.610
Stray dogs have their own ways of doing things.

00:22:35.610 --> 00:22:37.500
Joe, what are you...?

00:22:38.090 --> 00:22:42.210
There's still something we can do. It's a little risky, though.

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:45.030
It's something that'll make the boxing association accept us as pros...

00:22:46.770 --> 00:22:48.980
even if they don't want to!

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:54.320
Well, just watch for now.

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:58.480
You don't have to do anything. I'll build this bridge on my own!

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:34.600
The rookie tournament has begun.

00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:37.810
Having his dream of being a pro boxer obstructed,

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:41.140
Joe stands before the rookie champion, Wolf Kanagushi.

00:23:41.140 --> 00:23:43.560
The Cross Counter burns against Wolf Kanagushi.

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:49.530
Now, for Joe, the man who raises storms, which way is tomorrow!?
